        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 66-year-old male patient, admitted on 18th May 2019 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Spirometry supported the diagnosis of significant obstructive ventilatory impairment. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy and intravenous fluids. The patient responded well to treatment with improvement in respiratory function and oxygen saturation. He was discharged on 19th May 2019 in stable condition. Discharge medication includes inhaled bronchodilators and a tapering oral steroid course. We recommend close follow-up and review of his long-term COPD management. Please do not hesitate to contact us if you have any questions.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
